2. KaKs_Calculator 2.0 (not contained: orthologr runs the program and reads its output)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    orthologr runs the program KaKs_Calculator when it is installed and reads its output;
    kaks_calc_header() (R/substitutionrate.R) holds the column names of that output, an interface that
    orthologr reads.

    R/lwl_counts.R (kaks_transl_table(), kaks_lwl_tables(), kaks_lwl_counts()): independent implementation
    (clean room, see CLEANROOM.md in the source repository, branch chore/gpl2-cleanroom) from the published
    methods (Li, Wu & Luo 1985; Li 1993; Pamilo & Bianchi 1993; Tzeng, Pan & Li 2004), checked against
    KaKs_Calculator's output only; the genetic code tables are NCBI data. It contains no code derived from
    KaKs_Calculator. Earlier versions of these three functions (in R/substitutionrate.R, on this fork only,
    before the 0.6.0 release) were derived from KaKs_Calculator 2.0's source; they were removed.

    kaks_saturated() (R/substitutionrate.R) tests whether the logarithms of the Kimura two-parameter step of
    the LWL family are defined (1 - 2P - Q > 0 and 1 - 2Q > 0, Kimura 1980; Li, Wu & Luo 1985) from the counts
    above. Earlier notes recorded that this test follows the same step of KaKs_Calculator's LWL85::preProcess();
    it is the condition under which the published formula is defined, and it was not rewritten in the clean
    room.


